    {
      "body": "`tier2_backbone_lr_lora.ipynb` is written and validated. Here's what you have.\n\n## The notebook\n\n23 cells (12 markdown, 11 code), same shape as `noise_floor_runs.ipynb`. One configuration, one seed, ~43 min.\n\n| knob | Tier 1 | Tier 2 |\n|---|---|---|\n| `penultimate_linear_layer` | True | **False** |\n| `pooling` | class_token | **global_average** (kept, per your call) |\n| `dropout` | 0.2 | **0.3** |\n| LoRA `r` / `alpha` | 8 / 8 | **16 / 32** (scaling 1.0 \u2192 2.0) |\n| `learning_rate` | 1e-4 | **3e-4**, 10% warmup, cosine to 0 |\n| `accumulate_grad_batches` | 4 | **2** (12 steps/epoch) |\n| `max_epochs` | 5 | **10** (120 optimizer steps) |\n| `num_workers` | 4 | **8** |\n\nTrainable params move from 1,515,520 adapters + 1,642,241 head to **3,031,040 adapters + 1,281 head** \u2014 99.96% of the gradient now flows into the backbone instead of a head large enough to memorize 23 examples. That's the experiment: can a 1,281-parameter readout find chirality if the adapters may reshape what it reads?\n\nThe two design points I proposed are in cell 7: the head bias is initialized to the train prior (0.4783) with weights scaled \u00d70.1, applied *before* `apply_peft_lora` because PEFT's `ModulesToSaveWrapper` copies the module; and `probe_initial_predictions()` runs a 4-batch forward pass before training starts. The probe deliberately uses the **val** loader \u2014 `shuffle=False` and no generator, so a throwaway iterator can't perturb the train shuffle order.\n\nCell 4 asserts the Tier 1 baseline values are still in the YAML before applying any override, so if the config drifts again you get a named diff rather than a silently different experiment.\n\n## Validation\n\nAll executed against the notebook's own kernel (`/home/jovyan/envs/surya_ws/bin/python`):\n\n- Cells 0\u20136 ran for real: drift assert passes, param prediction 3,031,040 + 1,281 = 3,032,321, TRAIN_PRIOR = 0.4783\n- Cosine schedule: 0.083 \u2192 1.000 by step 11, monotone decay to 0.00021\n- Tiny-model structural check at D=64: `modules_to_save == ['head_unembed']` (`head_dropout` correctly skipped), `nglo = 0`, head params 65 \u2192 1,281 at D=1280. Tier 1 contrast: `['head_cls_token','head_linear','head_unembed']`, 4,289 \u2192 1,642,241\n- Forward/backward: `out.shape == (3,)`, preds mean 0.4887 std 0.0077, probe **MSE 0.2505** \u2014 the run starts sitting exactly on the 0.2524 collapse floor, which is the point. Gradient reaches both `blocks_attention[0].mlp.fc1.weight` (|grad| sum 3.387) and `head_unembed`\n- All three verdict branches tested at synthetic 0.18 / 0.2495 / 0.40; the verdict cell reads the floor from the catalog and Tier 1's 0.248884 from `noise_floor_summary.csv` rather than hardcoding either\n\nRuntime is measured, not estimated: `version_3` metrics.csv spans 1244 s for 5 epochs over 34 sample-passes/epoch = 7.3 s/sample. One sample is ~1 GB and the cache is EFS at ~140 MB/s \u2248 7.2 s \u2014 the run is **I/O-bound**, so every model knob above is free in wall-clock terms. 10 epochs \u2248 43 min, \u00b130% (unrelated files were downloading during the measured run).\n\n## What to watch in the first ~2 minutes\n\nThe probe prints before training starts, and it's your early abort signal:\n\n- `std \u2248 0` \u2192 the head collapsed at init; something is wrong with the bias write\n- `mean` far from 0.4783 \u2192 the bias init didn't take (check it ran before `apply_peft_lora`)\n- `MSE` above 0.5 \u2192 worse than guessing; stop rather than wait 43 min\n\nIf the probe looks like 0.48 / small std / ~0.25, let it run.\n\n## Cleanup\n\n50 orphaned `*.partial*` files deleted (newest timestamped 13:09, before the ~14:2x container restart; embedded PIDs dead; no live downloader). 28 GB freed. All 8,804 complete `.nc` files untouched \u2014 nothing outside the unfinished downloads was removed.\n\nTwo things still on the table from earlier, neither touched: the stale train==val `WARNING` block at `configs/config_script.yaml:41-44`, and `3_finetune_template_1D.py`, which still imports from `downstream_apps.template.*` and fails on `filament_index_path`.",
